   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualifications for\nholding certain offices in the village of Northville in Fulton County",
    "basePrintNo": "S4715",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4715-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4715\n\nSPONSOR: TEDISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualifications\nfor holding certain offices in the village of Northville in Fulton Coun-\nty\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis Legislation will create additional penalties and fines for those or\nkilling an innocent bystander during an attack convicted of injuring on\nan elected official.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Section 3 of the public officers law is amended by adding a\nnew subdivision 71 to read as follows:\n\n71. In the village of Northville, in the county of Fulton, the\nProvisions of this section requiring a person to be a resident of.  the\nPolitical subdivision or municipal corporation of the state for which he\nor she shall be chosen or within which his or her official functions are\nrequired to be exercised, shall not prevent a person from holding the\noffice of treasurer, village clerk and code enforcement officer,\nprovided that such person resides in Fulton county, or in the town of\nEdinburg in Saratoga county or the town of Benson in Hamilton county;\nprovided, however that any person performing such functions or holding\nsuch office in any other village shall be a resident of such village\nunless otherwise provided by law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Village of Northville in Fulton County currently has flexibility\nwith hired positions such as Highway Superintendent. With appointed\npositions however, they do not have the same flexibility. Their\nappointed positions include Treasurer, Village Clerk and Code Enforce-\nment Officer. Northville is uniquely positioned on the border of both\nHamilton and Saratoga Counties.\n\nThe impetus for this legislation was the Village's high rate of turnover\nat key appointed positions (five code enforcement officers within a\nseven-year period). These setbacks are damaging to the stability and\ninfrastructure of a community.  Furthermore, a high turnover of person-\nnel is extremely costly to local governments, particularly at a time\nwhen our localities are facing fiscal challenges due to the COVID 19\npandemic.\n\nThis legislation would enable the Mayor of Northville to draw from a\nlarger pool for appointed positions, while staying within bordering\ntowns inside the Adirondack Park community.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
