    "lawCode": "Amd §3-300, Vil L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Village Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S4715A\n\nSPONSOR: TEDISCO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation\nto qualifications for holding certain offices in the village of North-\nville in Fulton county\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nRelates to the qualifications for holding appointed positions in the\nvillage of Northville on Fulton County\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1- Section 3-300 of the village law is amended by adding a new\nsubdivision 31 to read as follows:\n\n31. Notwithstanding any provisions of this chapter or any other chapter,\ngeneral law, local law, ordinance, or special act, the village board of\ntrustees of the incorporated village of Northville, Fulton county, may,\nby resolution, provide that the office treasurer, village clerk, and\ncode enforcement officer of such village may be held by a person who is\nnot a resident of such village, provided that such person resides within\nFulton county or an adjoining county within the state of New York.\n\nSection 2- Section 3 of the public officer's law is amended by adding a\nnew subdivision 71 to read as follows:\n\n71. In the village of Northville, in the county of Fulton, the\nprovisions of this section requiring a person to be a resident of the\npolitical subdivision or municipal corporation of the state for which he\nor she shall be chosen or within which his or her official functions are\nrequired to be exercised, shall not prevent a person from holding the\noffice treasurer, village clerk, and code enforcement officer of the\nvillage of Northville, provided that such person resides within Fulton\ncounty or an adjoining county within the state of New York. Provided,\nhowever, the person performing the functions of treasurer, village\nclerk, and code enforcement officer in any other village shall be a\nresident of such village unless otherwise provided by an act of the\nstate legislature.\n\nSection 3- This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n \nDIFFERENCE BETWEEN ORIGINAL AND AMENDED VERSION:\n\nAdds: Section 1- Section 3-300 of the village law is amended by adding a\nnew subdivision 31 to read as above.\n\nChanges Section 2- Section 3 of the public officer's law is amended by\nadding a new subdivision 71 to expend the area in which the a person\nperforming the functions of the positions in the village of Northville\nstated in this section to include all of Fulton county or an adjoining\ncounty within New York state.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\n\nThe Village of Northville in Fulton County currently has flexibility\nwith hired positions such as Highway Superintendent. With appointed\npositions however, they do not have the same flexibility. Their\nappointed positions include Treasurer, Village Clerk and Code Enforce-\nment Officer. Northville is uniquely positioned on the border of both\nHamilton and Saratoga Counties.\n\nThe impetus for this legislation was the Village's high rate of turnover\nat key appointed positions (five code enforcement officers within a\nseven-year period). These setbacks are damaging to the stability and\ninfrastructure of a community.\n\nFurthermore, a high turnover of personnel is extremely costly to local\ngovernments, particularly at a time when our localities are facing\nfiscal challenges due to the COVID 19 pandemic.\n\nThis legislation would enable the Mayor of Northville to draw from a\nlarger pool for appointed positions, while staying within bordering\ntowns inside the Adirondack Park community.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone noted.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
